@page "/"

<PageTitle>FlociLab OCI</PageTitle>

<h1>FlociLab OCI</h1>

<p class="lede">
    OCI samples only — this app references <code>FlociLab.Core</code> and
    <code>FlociLab.Oci.ObjectStorage.Demo</code> and nothing else, so it is the standalone
    artifact: clone <code>hosts/FlociLab.Oci.Web</code> plus the samples it references and you have
    an OCI demo with no other cloud SDK anywhere in the dependency tree.
</p>

<p>
    <a class="button" href="/coverage">Open the coverage matrix →</a>
</p>

<h2>The emulator</h2>

<table class="grid">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th>Cloud</th>
            <th>Image</th>
            <th>Endpoint</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td>OCI</td><td><code>floci/floci-oci</code></td><td><code>http://localhost:4599</code></td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<p class="note">
    The Floci web console has no OCI support at all, verified against the shipped binary — this app
    is the only place these samples are visible.
</p>

<p class="note">
    The endpoint comes from the <code>Floci:Oci</code> configuration section, and already defaults
    to the emulator's published port — so this app needs no configuration at all as long as
    <code>floci/floci-oci</code> is running. The Aspire AppHost starts that container but does not run this
    host: it wires its live endpoints into <code>FlociLab.All.Web</code> only. Running inside the
    Compose network means setting <code>Floci__Oci__Endpoint=http://floci-oci:4599</code>.
</p>
